    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "BRANCHING\n\nBranch is the if/else of Blueprints: it has ONE exec input and TWO exec outputs, True and False.\nOnly the wire that matches the Condition runs. Nest branches to choose among more than two outcomes\n(or use Multi Branch / Switch, shown in other examples). Here the temperature picks a label.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. FIRST QUESTION\nIs the temperature greater than 30? Greater Than outputs a boolean that is wired into Branch.Condition. True: it is hot. False: ask the next question.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          680.0
        ],
        "size": [
          760.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "t1",
          "hot_q",
          "br1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. SECOND QUESTION\nOnly reached when the first answer was False. Below 10 is cold, anything else is mild. With temperature = 25 the label ends up \"mild\".",
        "position": [
          660.0,
          810.0
        ],
        "size": [
          760.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "t2",
          "cold_q",
          "br2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "OUTCOMES\nEach outcome stores a label and prints a line. Exactly one of the three runs.",
        "position": [
          960.0,
          -60.0
        ],
        "size": [
          560.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.3,
          0.75,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "is_hot",
          "say_hot"
        ]
      }
